            <div xml:id="d935">

                <pb facs="0976" n="968" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg968"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">540.61B3/269: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-11T13:00:00-04:00">September 11, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>105. Your 188, September 10, 10 p.m. For Everett.</p>
                <pb facs="0977" n="969" xml:id="pg969"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>A procès-verbal as explained in 188 is acceptable to this
                        Government</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>It is important that the procès-verbal should be in form for signature on
                        the part of countries which have signed but not ratified the Convention of
                        1933, in conformity with paragraphs 2 and 3 of Department’s 103 of September
                        9, 4 p.m., as well as in form for signature on the part of countries which
                        are already bound by the Convention by ratification or definitive
                        adherence.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The Department understands that of the signatory countries of the
                        Convention, Albania, Finland, France, Panama, and Uruguay as well as the
                        United States have not ratified. The representatives of these countries at
                        the conference might associate themselves with you in regard to the point
                        covered by paragraph 2 of this telegram.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
